WEBVTT

1
00:00:55.657 --> 00:00:58.493
<i><font color="#804040">(man)</font> Everyone in town
always took me for an outsider.</i>

2
00:00:58.660 --> 00:01:00.370
<i>I didn't care.</i>

3
00:01:00.537 --> 00:01:03.498
<i>The only thing that mattered was her.</i>

4
00:01:03.665 --> 00:01:05.333
<i>She was my Garden of Eden,</i>

5
00:01:05.500 --> 00:01:08.920
<i>and God knows how beautiful it was
until that night.</i>

6
00:01:09.087 --> 00:01:11.089
<i>You know, no one is born evil.</i>

7
00:01:11.256 --> 00:01:13.216
<i>The Devil himself was a fallen angel.</i>

8
00:01:13.383 --> 00:01:15.927
<i>But sometimes,
when you go through hell,</i>

9
00:01:16.094 --> 00:01:18.972
<i>the only way out
is to walk deeper into the fire.</i>

10
00:01:19.139 --> 00:01:20.515
Are you horny?

11
00:01:21.558 --> 00:01:23.310
Yeah, I'm getting warmer.

12
00:01:23.476 --> 00:01:24.603
<font color="#804040">(laughs)</font>

13
00:01:25.228 --> 00:01:26.271
Fine.

14
00:01:26.438 --> 00:01:27.564
<font color="#804040">(both laugh)</font>

15
00:01:27.939 --> 00:01:30.191
- No.
- Yes.

16
00:01:34.070 --> 00:01:36.031
<font color="#804040">(giggling)</font>

17
00:01:43.622 --> 00:01:46.708
I'm gonna love you
for the rest of my life.

18
00:01:50.795 --> 00:01:53.506
Just love me
for the rest of mine.

19
00:01:58.428 --> 00:02:01.056
<font color="#804040">(rumbling)</font>

20
00:02:27.248 --> 00:02:28.249
<font color="#804040">(groans)</font>

21
00:03:20.176 --> 00:03:22.345
<font color="#804040">(♪ David Bowie: "Heroes")</font>

22
00:04:03.928 --> 00:04:05.430
<font color="#804040">(people shouting)</font>

23
00:04:05.597 --> 00:04:08.183
<font color="#804040">(man)</font> Oh, here he is...

24
00:04:10.351 --> 00:04:13.313
<font color="#804040">(record slows to a distorted stop)</font>

25
00:04:20.445 --> 00:04:23.531
<font color="#804040">(man in slow motion)</font> Murderer!

26
00:04:23.698 --> 00:04:25.784
<font color="#804040">(people continue clamoring)</font>

27
00:04:27.619 --> 00:04:29.871
Hey, Ig, what does it feel like
to get away with murder?

28
00:04:30.038 --> 00:04:32.749
Do you want to comment on the fire
at the lab in Tacoma last night?

29
00:04:32.916 --> 00:04:34.584
Have you heard
that the police have a new witness?

30
00:04:34.751 --> 00:04:37.712
You should ask God to save your soul
for what you did to her!

31
00:04:37.879 --> 00:04:40.840
I should ask the Devil
to punish whoever the fuck killed her.

32
00:04:41.007 --> 00:04:43.551
- <font color="#804040">(man)</font> Murderer!
- <font color="#804040">(woman)</font> Rapist!

33
00:04:50.475 --> 00:04:52.393
<font color="#804040">(car tires screeching)</font>

34
00:05:01.903 --> 00:05:03.822
<font color="#804040">(phone line ringing)</font>

35
00:05:04.781 --> 00:05:06.908
<i><font color="#804040">(man)</font> Hi, this is Lee Tourneau,
leave a message.</i>

36
00:05:07.075 --> 00:05:11.538
Hi, Lee, please, can you meet me at
my parents' house in like half an hour?

37
00:05:11.704 --> 00:05:14.499
I really need to talk to you. Start
picking up your phone, man, come on.

38
00:05:26.719 --> 00:05:28.137
Are you proud of me, Mom?

39
00:05:28.304 --> 00:05:30.849
I'm so famous,
people follow me everywhere I go.

40
00:05:32.267 --> 00:05:34.519
Come inside, sweetie.

41
00:05:34.686 --> 00:05:37.272
<font color="#804040">(man)</font> You just can't talk
to those reporters.

42
00:05:37.438 --> 00:05:39.858
They'll take whatever you say
and just twist it around.

43
00:05:40.024 --> 00:05:43.653
But if I don't talk to them, it looks
like I have something to hide, right?

44
00:05:45.363 --> 00:05:48.241
How's Lee working out for you?
You still think he's up to the job?

45
00:05:48.408 --> 00:05:51.452
Yes, he's keeping me out of jail,
at least for the time being,

46
00:05:51.619 --> 00:05:53.788
and that's gotta be
some kind of triumph.

47
00:05:53.955 --> 00:05:56.249
All right, look,
I know he's an old friend of yours,

48
00:05:56.416 --> 00:05:58.585
but you don't have to settle
for a public defender.

49
00:05:58.751 --> 00:06:01.296
I've got the money, I will hire you
the best lawyer in Seattle.

50
00:06:01.462 --> 00:06:03.715
Dad, every other lawyer we talked to
wanted me to take a plea.

51
00:06:03.882 --> 00:06:06.843
Lee is the only one
who believes I'm innocent.

52
00:06:07.844 --> 00:06:09.888
<font color="#804040">(father sighs)</font>

53
00:06:10.054 --> 00:06:12.432
Just don't talk to
any more reporters, please.

54
00:06:12.599 --> 00:06:13.808
And don't admit anything.

55
00:06:13.975 --> 00:06:17.312
I don't have anything
to admit to, Dad.

56
00:06:19.147 --> 00:06:24.152
Look, honey, we don't care
what happened. You're our son.

57
00:06:24.319 --> 00:06:26.279
That's all that matters.

58
00:06:29.741 --> 00:06:31.910
- Oh, sit back down, Ig.
- If you think for a second

59
00:06:32.076 --> 00:06:34.871
that I might've killed her,
then why are you protecting me?

60
00:06:36.247 --> 00:06:39.751
Because if I did anything to her,
then I'm a fucking monster.

61
00:06:48.676 --> 00:06:51.387
- I got it, Mom.
- <font color="#804040">(father)</font> Thanks, Terry.

62
00:06:52.680 --> 00:06:56.976
<font color="#804040">(playing soulful tune)</font>

63
00:07:24.087 --> 00:07:26.506
Ig, look, I...

64
00:07:26.673 --> 00:07:29.217
I don't have to go back on the road
next week if you don't want me to.

65
00:07:29.384 --> 00:07:32.428
Man, you gotta earn a living.
I'll sort things out.

66
00:07:32.595 --> 00:07:34.555
Except I need you to stay, Terry.

67
00:07:35.473 --> 00:07:39.227
Whole family's gotta put up
a united front for Ig. Hey, buddy.

68
00:07:39.394 --> 00:07:40.728
How is it going?

69
00:07:40.895 --> 00:07:42.146
- Lee.
- Hey.

70
00:07:43.231 --> 00:07:44.273
Lee?

71
00:07:44.440 --> 00:07:47.443
If you want some food,
we have a lot of leftovers from lunch.

72
00:07:47.610 --> 00:07:49.946
Oh, I grabbed something on the way over,
Mrs. P., thank you.

73
00:07:50.822 --> 00:07:53.199
- How you guys doing?
- Yeah, um...

74
00:07:53.366 --> 00:07:55.451
Lee, what happened
at the lab in Tacoma?

75
00:07:55.618 --> 00:07:57.704
One of the reporters this morning
told me it burned down.

76
00:07:57.870 --> 00:08:00.498
Yeah. All the samples
from Merrin's body were destroyed.

77
00:08:00.665 --> 00:08:03.126
It's gonna be tough to recover
any blood or DNA at this point.

78
00:08:03.292 --> 00:08:05.628
That's a fucking disaster
for us, right?

79
00:08:05.795 --> 00:08:07.588
That means there's no evidence
anyone else killed her.

80
00:08:07.755 --> 00:08:11.592
It's not ideal, but I think it's
too early to panic at this point.

81
00:08:11.759 --> 00:08:14.178
And who is this new witness?
What is that?

82
00:08:14.345 --> 00:08:16.055
I'm trying to figure that out today,

83
00:08:16.222 --> 00:08:18.599
and I'm also getting your confession
to the police thrown out.

84
00:08:18.766 --> 00:08:20.435
Yeah, good.
You know I never confessed to them.

85
00:08:20.601 --> 00:08:22.603
They're just looking
for any way to put me away

86
00:08:22.770 --> 00:08:23.896
for the rest of my life.

87
00:08:24.063 --> 00:08:26.733
Whoa, whoa, whoa. It's OK.
Lee can fix anything, right?

88
00:08:27.358 --> 00:08:30.695
We'll see about that. But, you know,
you don't have to convince me.

89
00:08:30.862 --> 00:08:33.781
Ig, I believe you.

90
00:08:33.948 --> 00:08:36.200
You don't think
I'm capable of murder?

91
00:08:36.367 --> 00:08:39.370
Just put me in a room with the guy
who really killed her.

92
00:08:47.378 --> 00:08:50.965
<font color="#804040">(man)</font> Neighbor hears him say,
"Martha, Martha, hose me down."

93
00:08:51.132 --> 00:08:52.550
<font color="#804040">(men laughing)</font>

94
00:08:55.011 --> 00:08:56.304
No, but... And you know what?

95
00:08:56.471 --> 00:08:58.514
Little early for you
to start drinking, ain't it, Ig?

96
00:08:58.681 --> 00:09:00.850
They put me on leave
at the station.

97
00:09:01.017 --> 00:09:04.062
Apparently, most commuters don't like it
when their DJ is a murder suspect.

98
00:09:04.228 --> 00:09:09.108
Yeah, so maybe you should
take your business elsewhere.

99
00:09:09.275 --> 00:09:12.612
No offense, but you make
the other customers uncomfortable.

100
00:09:14.363 --> 00:09:16.532
You telling me I make these guys
feel uncomfortable?

101
00:09:17.366 --> 00:09:20.244
All right, come on, Iggy deserves
a drink as much as anybody.

102
00:09:20.411 --> 00:09:21.704
Thank you.

103
00:09:23.122 --> 00:09:24.791
More than anybody.

104
00:09:27.126 --> 00:09:29.128
Sorry you have to, like,

105
00:09:29.295 --> 00:09:31.506
stand up for me
all the time now, Glenna.

106
00:09:32.924 --> 00:09:34.258
<font color="#804040">(sighs)</font>

107
00:09:35.885 --> 00:09:38.805
Listen, Ig, if you're looking for
a friendlier place to grab a drink,

108
00:09:38.971 --> 00:09:40.431
I get off at 5:00.

109
00:09:40.598 --> 00:09:41.599
Um...

110
00:09:41.766 --> 00:09:44.769
I appreciate the offer, but I...

111
00:09:44.936 --> 00:09:49.232
...I'm probably better off, like,
drinking alone.

112
00:10:17.760 --> 00:10:19.387
<font color="#804040">(man)</font> Thank you all
for coming tonight

113
00:10:19.554 --> 00:10:22.390
to pay tribute to our dear girl,
Merrin.

114
00:10:23.933 --> 00:10:28.271
I know that Dale would like to say
a few words to welcome you.

115
00:10:30.773 --> 00:10:32.191
Well, uh...

116
00:10:33.734 --> 00:10:35.278
It's...

117
00:10:36.737 --> 00:10:38.281
It's real good to see you all here.

118
00:10:40.449 --> 00:10:42.869
The truth is I haven't felt much like

119
00:10:43.035 --> 00:10:45.913
getting out of bed in the morning
since Merrin...

120
00:10:51.043 --> 00:10:52.837
Ig Perrish...

121
00:10:54.088 --> 00:10:57.758
...he murdered her
and he is still walking the streets.

122
00:10:59.719 --> 00:11:04.015
I treated him like a son
practically all his life,

123
00:11:04.182 --> 00:11:05.975
and then he killed my little...

124
00:11:10.980 --> 00:11:12.815
...my little girl.

125
00:11:16.527 --> 00:11:20.448
As long as he is free, there is no way
that her soul can be laid to rest.

126
00:11:20.615 --> 00:11:22.783
<font color="#804040">(crying)</font>

127
00:11:22.950 --> 00:11:26.746
So let us all bow our heads in prayer.

128
00:11:40.885 --> 00:11:43.804
- Thank you for coming.
- <font color="#804040">(man)</font> Thank you, everybody.

129
00:12:00.863 --> 00:12:02.907
<font color="#804040">(panting)</font>

130
00:12:23.761 --> 00:12:25.137
<font color="#804040">(screams)</font>

131
00:12:38.818 --> 00:12:40.778
<font color="#804040">(grunting)</font>

132
00:12:45.032 --> 00:12:47.702
<font color="#804040">(panting)</font>

133
00:12:54.500 --> 00:12:57.545
- <font color="#804040">(chuckling)</font>
- Christ, Ig!

134
00:12:58.546 --> 00:13:00.589
Leave me alone, Glenna.

135
00:13:00.756 --> 00:13:02.925
What are you thinking,
coming out here?

136
00:13:03.092 --> 00:13:04.844
People could've seen you.

137
00:13:05.011 --> 00:13:08.222
She went to church
every fucking Sunday!

138
00:13:08.389 --> 00:13:10.891
She wore a cross around her neck.

139
00:13:13.144 --> 00:13:16.355
And did it make any difference? No.

140
00:13:17.189 --> 00:13:21.777
God turned a blind eye, and let her die
out here alone and afraid.

141
00:13:26.324 --> 00:13:29.285
- Come on. Oh, come on, Ig.
- Fucking God!

142
00:13:52.266 --> 00:13:55.478
<i><font color="#804040">(Ig)</font> For whatever reason
in this crazy, fucked up world</i>

143
00:13:55.644 --> 00:13:57.980
<i>I was being punished.</i>

144
00:13:58.147 --> 00:14:01.275
<i>When they looked at me,
they saw a devil.</i>

145
00:14:01.442 --> 00:14:03.110
<i>And maybe I did, too.</i>

146
00:14:05.988 --> 00:14:08.407
<i>And now,
I had to look the part.</i>

147
00:14:08.574 --> 00:14:10.034
<font color="#804040">(flies buzzing)</font>

148
00:14:16.916 --> 00:14:18.626
<font color="#804040">(crackling sounds)</font>

149
00:14:42.983 --> 00:14:45.319
Oh, shit.

150
00:15:08.509 --> 00:15:11.220
What the fuck?

151
00:15:22.481 --> 00:15:23.816
What...

152
00:15:32.116 --> 00:15:33.951
- <font color="#804040">(loud cracking)</font>
- <font color="#804040">(exclaims in pain)</font>

153
00:15:37.371 --> 00:15:39.540
<i><font color="#804040">(laughing)</font></i>

154
00:15:40.749 --> 00:15:44.044
<i>Let me have him!
Send him down!</i>

155
00:15:44.211 --> 00:15:46.464
<i>Give him to me now!</i>

156
00:15:46.630 --> 00:15:49.133
You were in the bathroom
for a long time.

157
00:15:51.302 --> 00:15:53.345
You still drunk?

158
00:15:54.138 --> 00:15:57.224
How do I look?
Do you notice anything unusual?

159
00:15:59.810 --> 00:16:01.020
You mean the horns?

160
00:16:01.187 --> 00:16:03.063
Shit, so they're real?

161
00:16:04.231 --> 00:16:05.274
Fuck!

162
00:16:07.443 --> 00:16:08.986
Hey, Ig?

163
00:16:10.070 --> 00:16:13.407
Can I...
Can I have another donut?

164
00:16:13.574 --> 00:16:15.159
Why are you asking me?

165
00:16:16.160 --> 00:16:18.913
One, two, three,

166
00:16:19.079 --> 00:16:22.416
four, five, six.

167
00:16:23.667 --> 00:16:26.337
Do you think it'd be OK
if I had six more donuts?

168
00:16:26.504 --> 00:16:29.006
Yeah, do whatever you like.

169
00:16:29.173 --> 00:16:30.925
Thank you.

170
00:16:54.323 --> 00:16:55.324
Mmm...

171
00:17:03.791 --> 00:17:04.792
Mmm-mmm.

172
00:17:08.629 --> 00:17:10.422
I didn't like it.

173
00:17:13.217 --> 00:17:15.052
My stomach hurts.

174
00:17:20.808 --> 00:17:21.892
Should I have another one?

175
00:17:22.059 --> 00:17:24.520
Why would you have another one
if your stomach hurts, Glenna?

176
00:17:24.687 --> 00:17:26.939
Because I want to get really fat.

177
00:17:27.690 --> 00:17:29.108
I'm worthless anyways.

178
00:17:29.275 --> 00:17:32.444
Nobody will screw me
without being totally drunk.

179
00:17:32.611 --> 00:17:34.697
Everybody in this town
thinks that I'm trash.

180
00:17:34.863 --> 00:17:36.949
<font color="#804040">(scoffs)</font> Come on, Glenna,
that's not true.

181
00:17:37.116 --> 00:17:39.994
You wouldn't have screwed me
if you weren't blind drunk.

182
00:17:40.160 --> 00:17:41.328
Well...

183
00:17:41.495 --> 00:17:44.582
And I know you were thinking
about Merrin the whole time.

184
00:17:44.748 --> 00:17:46.834
Hmm...

185
00:17:47.001 --> 00:17:49.795
Glenna, I'm sorry,
I've no excuse for last night.

186
00:17:49.962 --> 00:17:53.173
I just need to know
if I can eat the rest of this box.

187
00:17:53.340 --> 00:17:55.676
Yeah, go ahead, pig out.

188
00:17:58.387 --> 00:17:59.388
Uh...

189
00:17:59.638 --> 00:18:01.307
I think I'm just gonna go, Glenna.

190
00:18:01.473 --> 00:18:03.017
<font color="#804040">(muttering)</font>

191
00:18:03.183 --> 00:18:04.351
All right.

192
00:18:20.868 --> 00:18:25.372
<font color="#804040">(screaming loudly)</font>

193
00:18:25.789 --> 00:18:29.501
<font color="#804040">(woman)</font> Be quiet! I said, stop it!

194
00:18:29.668 --> 00:18:31.920
Sit over there and read your book.

195
00:18:32.087 --> 00:18:33.756
- Hi.
- What can I do for you?

196
00:18:33.922 --> 00:18:38.761
Yeah, I need Dr. Renald
to look at... something.

197
00:18:40.846 --> 00:18:42.514
Well...

198
00:18:43.641 --> 00:18:46.101
...that sure doesn't look right.

199
00:18:47.353 --> 00:18:49.605
I'm gonna need you
to fill out some forms.

200
00:18:50.439 --> 00:18:52.358
<font color="#804040">(girl screaming)</font>

201
00:18:57.446 --> 00:18:59.156
Stop it!

202
00:19:00.407 --> 00:19:03.285
I said, be quiet!
Go over there and read your book.

203
00:19:04.620 --> 00:19:05.621
Growth.

204
00:19:07.748 --> 00:19:09.917
You know,
for what it's worth,

205
00:19:10.084 --> 00:19:14.046
I'd like to kick my daughter
right in her spoiled ass.

206
00:19:16.590 --> 00:19:19.385
- Do you think I should?
- No, of course not.

207
00:19:19.551 --> 00:19:21.261
Of course...
Why would you even ask me that?

208
00:19:21.428 --> 00:19:22.805
<font color="#804040">(screams)</font>

209
00:19:22.971 --> 00:19:26.558
Well, maybe I should just
leave her here and drive away.

210
00:19:26.725 --> 00:19:29.103
Divorce my husband. <font color="#804040">(gasps)</font>

211
00:19:30.854 --> 00:19:34.650
- I could fuck my golf pro again.
- Excuse me?

212
00:19:34.817 --> 00:19:37.027
I'd never been with a jigaboo before,

213
00:19:37.194 --> 00:19:40.489
but it's true what they say
about black cocks.

214
00:19:40.656 --> 00:19:42.741
I call it my five iron.

215
00:19:43.158 --> 00:19:45.661
<font color="#804040">(girl screaming)</font>

216
00:19:47.371 --> 00:19:48.372
Here you go.

217
00:19:48.539 --> 00:19:51.917
I feel like I have to yell
at that girl's mother.

218
00:19:52.084 --> 00:19:55.212
I know it's not her fault that
her daughter's a screechy puke,

219
00:19:55.379 --> 00:19:56.755
but really, now.

220
00:19:57.589 --> 00:20:00.050
Go ahead. Why not?

221
00:20:01.427 --> 00:20:05.264
Ma'am? Do you think you could
show some fucking consideration

222
00:20:05.431 --> 00:20:06.724
and take your daughter out of here

223
00:20:06.890 --> 00:20:09.059
so we don't have
to listen to her screaming?

224
00:20:10.352 --> 00:20:11.895
What did you just say to me?

225
00:20:12.062 --> 00:20:15.983
I said you should take that
screeching pig of yours by the hair

226
00:20:16.150 --> 00:20:18.610
and drag her the fuck out of here!

227
00:20:18.777 --> 00:20:22.281
Fuck you!
Shut the hell up, you dried-up old twat!

228
00:20:22.448 --> 00:20:25.826
Hey, you don't want to do this
in front of your daughter. Come on...

229
00:20:31.248 --> 00:20:33.959
<font color="#804040">(woman groaning)</font>

230
00:20:36.628 --> 00:20:38.130
<font color="#804040">(screaming)</font>

231
00:20:39.423 --> 00:20:41.049
