511
00:41:17.952 --> 00:41:21.831
Just say it,
and we'll get it out of the way.

512
00:41:23.749 --> 00:41:25.793
I don't know
why you turned out like this.

513
00:41:28.546 --> 00:41:32.258
With your brother, it's easier.

514
00:41:35.219 --> 00:41:36.804
We could always play music together.

515
00:41:36.971 --> 00:41:40.558
But with you,
I never know what to say to you.

516
00:41:40.725 --> 00:41:46.272
Well... that's not bad,
all things considered.

517
00:41:46.439 --> 00:41:48.691
I think about Merrin.

518
00:41:51.527 --> 00:41:54.321
What a beautiful girl she was.

519
00:42:01.162 --> 00:42:06.375
I loved her. You know, in a way.

520
00:42:08.794 --> 00:42:09.920
I envied you.

521
00:42:12.006 --> 00:42:13.507
I was never in love with anyone

522
00:42:13.674 --> 00:42:15.593
the way you two were in love
with each other.

523
00:42:15.760 --> 00:42:19.388
You couldn't hear her laugh
without smiling.

524
00:42:19.555 --> 00:42:21.307
It was like music.

525
00:42:23.184 --> 00:42:25.227
And when I think about
what you did to her...

526
00:42:25.394 --> 00:42:27.104
<font color="#804040">(scoffs)</font>

527
00:42:28.022 --> 00:42:32.985
And you never thought, maybe,
just maybe, that I didn't do it?

528
00:42:33.152 --> 00:42:35.404
Of course not.

529
00:42:35.571 --> 00:42:37.865
You're trying to
get away with murder.

530
00:42:38.032 --> 00:42:40.242
And the worst part is,
I'm helping you do it!

531
00:42:40.409 --> 00:42:42.995
What? What do you mean by that?

532
00:42:43.162 --> 00:42:46.332
I went to college with the guy
that runs the state forensics lab.

533
00:42:46.499 --> 00:42:49.418
Dad, are you telling me you got
your friend to set that fire at the lab?

534
00:42:49.585 --> 00:42:51.670
When the world comes for my son
with the knives out,

535
00:42:51.837 --> 00:42:54.381
it's my job to stand in the way!
And if you went to jail...

536
00:42:54.548 --> 00:42:56.801
Dad, the evidence you got burned up
could have saved me!

537
00:42:56.967 --> 00:42:58.677
How could you do it?

538
00:43:00.137 --> 00:43:02.681
She was one of the best people
I ever knew!

539
00:43:02.848 --> 00:43:07.394
She was my favorite thing about you.

540
00:43:08.437 --> 00:43:10.106
Yeah, me too.

541
00:43:11.232 --> 00:43:12.775
So if you knew how much I loved her,

542
00:43:12.942 --> 00:43:15.486
then how could you ever believe
I'd kill her?

543
00:43:20.449 --> 00:43:23.077
Isn't that why you killed her?

544
00:43:24.078 --> 00:43:26.622
Because you loved her so much?

545
00:43:28.415 --> 00:43:30.000
And you lost her.

546
00:43:32.586 --> 00:43:35.714
Way more people kill out of love
than out of hate.

547
00:43:36.423 --> 00:43:37.424
<font color="#804040">(crying)</font>

548
00:43:41.345 --> 00:43:44.098
<i><font color="#804040">(Lee)</font> What's going on, Ig?
You go home like I asked you to?</i>

549
00:43:44.265 --> 00:43:46.267
<font color="#804040">(Ig)</font> Yeah, I did that
and it was very enlightening.

550
00:43:46.433 --> 00:43:49.186
Did you know that my dad got
his friend to start the fire in the lab?

551
00:43:49.353 --> 00:43:50.437
<i><font color="#804040">(Lee)</font> Uh...</i>

552
00:43:50.604 --> 00:43:54.191
<i>Hypothetically, if I did know, I would
legally be required to tell the police.</i>

553
00:43:54.358 --> 00:43:58.070
<i>But maybe the fire
was a blessing in disguise.</i>

554
00:43:58.237 --> 00:44:01.574
How? How was it a fucking blessing?
If the lab hadn't burned down,

555
00:44:01.740 --> 00:44:03.409
that evidence would've cleared me, Lee!

556
00:44:03.576 --> 00:44:05.995
<i>OK, OK, I know it's rough for you
staying at your house right now.</i>

557
00:44:06.162 --> 00:44:08.497
<i>Why don't you just take the keys to
my place? You can crash on the couch.</i>

558
00:44:08.664 --> 00:44:11.625
No. You know what? I'm fine.
I've actually got a lot to do.

559
00:44:11.792 --> 00:44:14.545
I've gotta figure out who really
killed Merrin and get him to confess.

560
00:44:14.712 --> 00:44:16.338
<i>How you planning to do that?</i>

561
00:44:16.505 --> 00:44:19.133
Lately, I can be
pretty fucking persuasive.

562
00:44:31.353 --> 00:44:34.565
Hey, Ig, nice look for you.
Showing your true nature?

563
00:44:34.732 --> 00:44:36.734
I'd appreciate it
if you guys would all just fuck off.

564
00:44:36.901 --> 00:44:39.486
Come on, Ig, admit you killed her,
it'd be such a huge scoop for me.

565
00:44:39.653 --> 00:44:42.156
Good to know your journalistic integrity
is fucking unimpeachable.

566
00:44:42.323 --> 00:44:44.825
Hey, you confess to me,
I can get out of stupid local news.

567
00:44:44.992 --> 00:44:46.535
You know what?
I got an idea.

568
00:44:46.702 --> 00:44:49.038
How about you guys
beat the shit out of each other,

569
00:44:49.205 --> 00:44:51.498
